By successfully completing this course, you should be able to
 Understand key concepts related to intergovernmental relations, such as federal system, unitary system, and confederation, and how intergovernmental relations in both federal and unitary systems have evolved in the last 200 years;
 Be fully aware that all systems in the real world are somewhat mixed;
 Achieve a broader knowledge about various theories of inter-governmental relations;
 Think critically about the merits and problems of various forms of inter-governmental relations;
